#CHLOEAI:1
---
wisl_version: 1
folder: .
orient: "CANONICAL TEMPLATE: this repo is the authoritative pattern for new WylieH2S projects. It is NOT a live project — it defines the substrate skeleton that init-project.sh stamps out. Every structural decision here propagates fleet-wide when a new repo is initialized. The AI-job here is: maintaining the template + authoring the standards that downstream repos inherit."
owns:
  - "**"
depends_on: []
risk: >-
  TEMPLATE PROPAGATION TRAP: changes here do NOT automatically update existing
  repos — they only apply when a NEW repo is initialized via init-project.sh or
  when a repo manually adopts the updated pattern. If you update a substrate
  standard here (CLAUDE.md format, lefthook hooks, drift-sweep version), you must
  also plan fleet rollout or document the version delta. PLACEHOLDER SYNTAX: files
  use {{AI}} and {{HUMAN}} as template tokens (e.g. readme_AI.{{AI}}ai); do NOT
  expand these — they are expanded by init-project.sh at init time. The
  templateRepo_EXAMPLE itself keeps them unexpanded.
continuity: "templateRepo_EXAMPLE is TEMPLATE status in the ROSTER — read-only unless updating a fleet-wide standard. Substrate packs live in stacks/; the drift-sweep canonical skills live in ~/GitHub/.claude/skills/ (symlinked into active repos, not copied from here). validate-substrate and the standard lefthook hooks are the authoritative source here."
validation: "bash init-project.sh --dry-run 2>&1 | head -20  # if that flag exists; else: bash -n init-project.sh"
verified_at: "5b4ef75"
actors:
  cloud: write    # Claude maintains the template standards
  chloe-local: read
  codex: none
boot_path:
  - init-project.sh          # the stamper — how a new repo is initialized from this template
  - CLAUDE.md                # the Tier-1 path-rule table that all projects inherit
  - lefthook.yml             # standard pre-commit hooks (drift-sweep, validate-substrate, no-secrets)
  - ai_context/              # substrate scaffold (decisions/, glossary, ai_rules, START_HERE)
  - stacks/                  # optional stack packs (Swift, TS, Python, GBC) — pulled in at init
---
This is the pattern source, not an active project.

When working here:
- Editing CLAUDE.md or lefthook.yml means you're changing what every future
  repo gets. Think fleet-wide before committing.
- Placeholder files (readme_AI.{{AI}}ai, etc.) stay templated — init-project.sh
  expands them. Keep {{AI}} / {{HUMAN}} unexpanded.
- stacks/ contains opt-in language packs; changes there only affect repos that
  explicitly pull the stack at init or during a manual substrate update.
